   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">We invested INR 3.6 billion in Aavas in a social bond programme to help increase women?s access to finance and encourage ownership of properties in India. Our lending is specifically targeted towards increasing and promoting availability of finance for properties that must have women on the title-deed.Access to housing and ownership of property can have strong positive impact on safety, dignity, improved livelihoods, and better economic outcomes.This investment also qualifies under the 2X challenge, an initiative launched by the development finance institutions (DFIs) of the G7 to mobilise capital to support increased economic empowerment for women in emerging economies.</narrative>
   </description>
